codex
I have six candidates. Two have short proof routes for explicit special families; one looks worth auditing as an RH-conditional hyperelliptic result; three need new distribution estimates. The strongest general average-case target is \(N^{23/152+o(1)}\): an explicit ECM family would need only a second-moment separation bound, and the existing fourth-moment tail then controls fallback costs even if the failure sets overlap adversarially.

